Experiment 5: Implementation of Various Scheduling Mechanisms Using an Open-Source Cloud Simulator

📌 Overview:
This experiment demonstrates different scheduling mechanisms using CloudSim Plus, an open-source cloud simulation framework.

The experiment compares Virtual Machine (VM) scheduling and Cloudlet scheduling using two approaches:

Space Shared Scheduling
Time Shared Scheduling

Four different combinations of these scheduling mechanisms are implemented and executed.

.

🎯 Objectives

To understand scheduling mechanisms in cloud computing.
To implement Space Shared and Time Shared scheduling.
To compare different combinations of VM and Cloudlet scheduling.
To simulate cloud resource allocation and Cloudlet execution using CloudSim Plus.

🛠️ Technologies Used

Operating System: Ubuntu (Oracle VirtualBox)

Programming Language: Java 17

Cloud Simulator: CloudSim Plus 8.5.5

Build Tool: Apache Maven 3.9.12

Version Control: Git



# Experiment 5: Implementation of Various Scheduling Mechanisms Using an Open-Source Cloud Simulator

## 📌 Overview


## ⚙️ Environment Setup

### 1. Update Ubuntu

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
```

### 2. Install Java, Maven and Git

```bash
sudo apt install openjdk-17-jdk maven git -y
```

### 3. Verify installations

```bash
java -version
javac -version
mvn -version
git --version
```

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
CloudSchedulingLab/
│
├── pom.xml
│
└── src/
    └── main/
        └── java/
            └── lab/
                └── SchedulingExperiment.java
```

## 📦 Maven Dependency

The project uses CloudSim Plus version 8.5.5.

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.cloudsimplus</groupId>
    <artifactId>cloudsimplus</artifactId>
    <version>8.5.5</version>
</dependency>
```

## 🚀 Implementation Steps

### 1. Create the Maven project

```bash
mkdir -p ~/CloudSchedulingLab/src/main/java/lab
cd ~/CloudSchedulingLab
```

### 2. Resolve dependencies and clean the project

```bash
mvn dependency:resolve
mvn clean
```

### 3. Create the Java source file

```bash
nano src/main/java/lab/SchedulingExperiment.java
```

The Java program creates:
- One Datacenter
- One Host with four Processing Elements (PEs)
- Two Virtual Machines
- Four Cloudlets

### 4. Compile the program

```bash
mvn clean compile
```

### 5. Execute the simulation

```bash
mvn exec:java -Dexec.mainClass="lab.SchedulingExperiment" -Dexec.classpathScope=compile
```

If the Maven Exec plugin prefix is not resolved, use the fully qualified command:

```bash
mvn org.codehaus.mojo:exec-maven-plugin:3.5.0:java -Dexec.mainClass="lab.SchedulingExperiment" -Dexec.classpathScope=compile
```

## 📊 Scheduling Mechanisms Implemented

The experiment implements four scheduling combinations:

| Scenario | VM Scheduler | Cloudlet Scheduler |
|---|---|---|
| A | Space Shared | Space Shared |
| B | Space Shared | Time Shared |
| C | Time Shared | Space Shared |
| D | Time Shared | Time Shared |

### Scheduling Types

**1. Space Shared Scheduling**

Resources are allocated exclusively to a task or VM for the period of its execution. Other tasks may need to wait until the required resources become available.

**2. Time Shared Scheduling**

Available processing resources are shared among multiple tasks or VMs by allocating processing time to them.

