## ✅ Results and Observations

All four scheduling scenarios were executed successfully.

| Scenario | Completed Cloudlets | Execution Status |
|---|---:|---|
| A | 4/4 | SUCCESS |
| B | 4/4 | SUCCESS |
| C | 4/4 | SUCCESS |
| D | 4/4 | SUCCESS |

**Observations:**

- All four Cloudlets completed successfully in every scenario.
- The simulation displayed Cloudlet IDs, VM IDs, execution status, start time and finish time.
- The final Maven execution displayed `BUILD SUCCESS`.
- Resource availability warnings appeared during execution, but they did not prevent the Cloudlets from completing.

## 🏁 Conclusion

The experiment successfully demonstrated four combinations of VM and Cloudlet scheduling mechanisms using CloudSim Plus.

It helped understand how Space Shared and Time Shared scheduling approaches manage computing resources and execute Cloudlets in a simulated cloud environment.

**Final Outcome:** Successfully implemented, compiled and executed all four scheduling scenarios.

